    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Sterium features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Daily Spiritual Dashboard</p>

        <h3>See the spiritual context around today before you begin</h3>

        <p>
          Sterium's Home experience can surface the current moon phase and zodiac
          sign, illumination, moon day, moonrise and moonset, the next Sabbat,
          planetary day and hour, current correspondences, daily numerology,
          retrogrades and transits, lucky hours, and working-timing guidance.
          Home widgets can also be customized so the information you care about
          most appears first.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Current Moon</span>
          <span>Sabbats</span>
          <span>Planetary Hours</span>
          <span>Numerology</span>
          <span>Transits</span>
          <span>Working Timing</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Correspondences</p>

        <h3>Build a reference library that can be generated, edited, or written by hand</h3>

        <p>
          Browse correspondence categories, generate entries from a name, save
          results, edit them later, delete what you no longer need, or create
          custom entries manually. Sterium's correspondence records can hold
          practical associations ranging from intentions, planets, zodiac signs,
          elements, deities, chakras, numerology, Tarot, Sabbats, lunar phases,
          seasons, days, colors, symbols, ritual uses, folklore, warnings, and
          category-specific details.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Spells</p>

        <h3>Generate spellwork from intention, context, and practitioner level</h3>

        <p>
          Choose a spell category and intention, set an expertise level, describe
          the situation and desired outcome, and let Sterium generate a structured
          spell. You can also add spells manually, browse saved spells by category,
          edit generated work, replace it with your revisions, and remove spells
          you no longer want to keep.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Grimoire</p>

        <h3>Keep many kinds of spiritual records inside one searchable grimoire</h3>

        <p>
          Sterium supports journals, working documents, working results, dreams,
          synchronicities, pathwork, moon-phase entries, deity devotion,
          divination, meditation, shadow work, manifestation, experiences, and
          custom grimoire entries. Search across entries, filter by type, build
          custom filters, and manage custom templates for forms that match the
          way you personally document your practice.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Vision Boards</p>

        <h3>Turn inspiration into visual collections that stay inside your practice</h3>

        <p>
          Create multiple vision boards, give each one a name and description,
          collect images into them, and open dedicated board details when you want
          to work with a collection. Sterium's share extension also lets images
          arrive directly from places like Pinterest, Safari, Photos, and other
          sharing sources.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Events</p>

        <h3>Give meaningful dates and plans a dedicated spiritual calendar</h3>

        <p>
          Sterium's Events area uses one shared event store with Agenda, Timeline,
          and Calendar views. Create new events, open full event details, edit
          existing entries, and move between high-level calendar planning and
          date-focused timeline views without maintaining separate copies.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Events</span>
            <strong>One shared calendar</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Agenda</span>
            <span>Timeline</span>
            <span>Calendar</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Customizable Practice</p>

        <h2>Let the app adapt to the way you actually practice instead of forcing one fixed system</h2>

        <p>
          Sterium includes customization at several levels: reorder or hide Home
          widgets, build custom grimoire templates, create custom grimoire filters,
          add correspondences manually, add spells manually, and choose which
          parts of the system deserve the most attention in your own practice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Sterium customization preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Make It Yours</span>

        <h4>Shape Sterium around your practice.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Home</span>
          <strong>Choose and arrange daily widgets</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Grimoire</span>
          <strong>Create custom templates and filters</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Content</span>
          <strong>Add manual spells and correspondences</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Sterium experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Moon, Sabbats & Planetary Timing</b>
              <small>Follow the current lunar cycle and time ritual work more intentionally</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Home tracks the current moon phase, zodiac sign, illumination, moon
            day, moonrise and moonset, the next Sabbat with live countdown, and
            the planetary day and current planetary hour. Local planetary-hour
            calculations can use location when available.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Daily Correspondences, Numerology & Sky Events</b>
              <small>See today's symbolic context without assembling it manually</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Sterium can surface current planetary, elemental, color, crystal, and
            herb correspondences alongside daily numerology, Tarot archetype
            associations, retrogrades, and current astrological transits.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Lucky Hours & Working Timing</b>
              <small>Use daily timing information to plan spiritual work</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Lucky-hour calculations and the working-timing system help surface
            favorable windows and timing reasons for practice. Saved timing tools
            let useful results stay available beyond a single calculation.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Custom Grimoire Templates & Filters</b>
              <small>Design entry structures that match the way you document your practice</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Beyond Sterium's built-in grimoire types, custom templates let you
            define your own record structures, while custom filters make it easier
            to group the entry types that belong together for a particular focus.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Apple Shortcuts</b>
              <small>Pull key daily spiritual information into automations and voice workflows</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Sterium exposes App Shortcuts for the current moon, upcoming Sabbat,
            planetary day and hour, and current correspondences, making core daily
            information available outside the main app when building shortcuts.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Vision Board Sharing</b>
              <small>Send inspiration into Sterium from other apps</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Sterium includes a Share extension so visual inspiration can be sent
            directly into its vision-board system from external apps instead of
            requiring a separate import-and-organize step later.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Settings, Release Notes & Report Center</b>
              <small>Keep app information, feedback, and support tools inside Sterium</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Settings includes release notes and an in-app Report Center with
            dedicated flows for bug reports, beta feedback, and feature requests,
            keeping product feedback connected to the app itself.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around a Living Practice</p>

        <h2>Spiritual work changes from day to day, so the system around it should be able to change too.</h2>

        <p>
          Sterium is built around a practice that can include timing, study,
          ritual, reflection, divination, inspiration, planning, and recordkeeping
          in different proportions at different times. Each area has its own depth
          while remaining part of the same connected spiritual workspace.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Sterium</p>

      <h2>Keep the many parts of your spiritual practice within one connected space.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Sterium, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Sterium/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Sterium Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-sterium-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .sterium-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

